# Site copy

Any string a visitor, search engine, or AI engine reads is copy. For a full rewrite, follow `.cursor/skills/site-copywriting/SKILL.md`. Run `pnpm copy:check` before you finish.

## Voice

First person, Aris talking to one reader. Plain, direct, a bit blunt about limits. It reads like a senior developer explaining a trade-off, never like an agency.

## Hard rules

- No em dashes (—) or en dashes (–) in copy. Use a period, comma, colon, or parentheses.
- No not-X-but-Y contrasts ("not slide decks", "bukan tim besar", "it's not X, it's Y") unless the reader actually believes X.
- No invented facts. Numbers, clients, roles, and dates must already be on the site or in `authorProfile` (`lib/seo/config.ts`).
- Say what the reader gets. Replace a feature with an outcome, or cut it.
- CTA buttons name the next step and what the reader gets, for example "Send me your site", "Get Cursor mentoring for your team", or "Book a scoping call". Never "Get in touch", "Learn more", "Submit", or "Get started".
- Use sentence case for headings, chips, and buttons. Don't Title Case Every Word.
- No banned words: seamless, leverage, robust, cutting-edge, pixel-perfect, comprehensive, innovative, world-class, unlock, elevate, empower, supercharge, blazing, next-level, solutions (as a noun for what I sell), utilize, peak performance.

```tsx
// ❌ 'Pixel-perfect WordPress themes that capture your unique style.'
// ✅ 'A theme built from your design, fast on phones, easy for editors to update.'

// ❌ 'Agents and chatbots shipped into real products — not slide decks.'
// ✅ 'Agents and chatbots that run inside your Next.js product and reach real users.'
```
